{{Quote|I remember what it was like before your ships showed up, before you Imperials ruined Lothal like the rest of the galaxy.|Yoffar grows angry at Imperials harassing him|<ref name="Spark" />}}
'''Yoffar''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Gotal]] who worked peddling [[jogan fruit]] on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]] during the early [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Era|reign]]. On one occasion he was nearly arrested for treason by Imperial [[Commandant]] [[Cumberlayne Aresko]] and [[Taskmaster]] [[Myles Grint]] after criticising the Empire in front of them while they questioned him about his business. The Gotal was saved by the local street urchin [[Ezra Bridger]], who distracted the Imperials with a fake emergency broadcast.

==Biography==
{{Quote|I'm just trying to sell a couple jogans here.|Yoffar explains himself to the Imperials|<ref name="Spark" />}}
The [[Gotal]] [[Gender|male]] Yoffar<ref name="TRB">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Rebellion Begins]]''</ref> was a street [[merchant]] who lived on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]] during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Spark" /> By [[Lothal Calendar|Lothal Year]] 3272,<ref name="RVG">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> he was reasonably elderly and eked out a living selling [[Standard day|day]]-old [[jogan fruit]]s in Lothal's [[Capital City]]. He occasionally interacted with the local street urchin [[Ezra Bridger]], who sometimes stole from him, and on one occasion Yoffar falsely accused the boy of having taken a jogan when in fact he had not.<ref name="TRB" /> While peddling his goods, Yoffar was approached by Imperial [[Commandant]] [[Cumberlayne Aresko]] and [[Taskmaster]] [[Myles Grint]], who asked to see his identification and questioned him over the fact that his commerce had not been registered with the Empire.<ref name="Spark" /> The check was in fact part of a planned demonstration of the Empire's ability to respond swiftly to problems,<ref name="TRB" /> and when Yoffar criticized the Empire the pair prepared to arrest him for [[treason]], quickly summoning a pair of [[stormtrooper]]s.<ref name="Spark" />

[[File:Officers_Harass_Merchant.png|thumb|right|250px|Yoffar was nearly arrested for treason by the Empire.]]
Before the Imperials could remove Yoffar however, they were distracted by an emergency call from their [[comlink]]s summoning them to the main square, which caused them to abandon the street merchant. The Gotal noticed Bridger issuing the emergency Imperial broadcast on a communicator he had taken from Aresko, and thanked him for saving him from arrest. He offered the boy a jogan, which Bridger accepted before grabbing a few more [[fruit]]s and moving on.<ref name="Spark" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|By the time the Empire's done, there won't be any trade left.|Yoffar criticizes the Empire|<ref name="TRB" />}}
Yoffar had [[Color|white]] fur, gray skin, and orange [[eye]]s.<ref name="Spark" /> He was perpetually grumpy, and commonly confused Ezra Bridger with other street orphans, which caused the boy to dislike him.<ref name="TRB" /> When approached by Aresko and Grint, Yoffar was at first defiant, but soon became terrified when stormtroopers arrived to arrest him. He was thankful to Bridger for saving him, but still complained when the urchin took more fruit than he was offered.<ref name="Spark" />

==Behind the scenes==
Yoffar was created for the [[2014]] ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]'' television movie, which acted as the premiere for the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' television series.

